---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { pricing, pricingDisplay, formatPrice, estimateMonthlyCost } from '../../config/pricing';
import ContentsNav from '../../components/ContentsNav.astro';
import '../../styles/information.css';
import '../../styles/guides.css';
const examples = [100, 500, 1000].map((documents) => ({ documents, usage: formatPrice(documents * pricing.standard.documentFee), total: formatPrice(estimateMonthlyCost(documents)) }));
const contents = [
  ['price', 'The two-part price'],
  ['count', 'Count documents'],
  ['estimates', 'Monthly estimates'],
  ['questions', 'Questions to settle'],
] as const;
---
<BaseLayout title="How EDI costs work for suppliers | EDI Spark" description="Understand EDI Spark’s mailbox and document fees, estimate monthly document volume and see worked examples before choosing a service.">
  <SiteHeader current="/guides" />
  <main id="main-content" class="information-page guide-page">
    <header class="information-hero">
      <div class="information-wrap">
        <nav class="guide-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/guides">Supplier guides</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span aria-current="page">EDI costs</span></nav>
        <h1>How much will your EDI exchange cost?</h1>
        <p class="information-lede">Start with the monthly service fee, then count the business documents you expect to exchange. An order can generate several documents, so order count alone will understate usage.</p>
        <p class="guide-date">EDI Spark editorial · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-21">21 November 2026</time></p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="information-wrap information-body reading-layout">
      <ContentsNav items={contents} />
      <article class="information-prose">
        <section id="price"><h2>The standard price has two parts</h2><p>EDI Spark’s published standard price is {pricingDisplay.monthlyFee} per month for your mailbox, plus {pricingDisplay.documentFee} per business document exchanged. Prices exclude VAT. The published offer has a {pricing.standard.trialDays}-day free trial, a {formatPrice(pricing.standard.setupFee)} setup fee and no annual contract.</p><p class="guide-formula"><span>Recurring estimate</span> <strong>{pricingDisplay.monthlyFee} + (monthly documents × {pricingDisplay.documentFee})</strong></p><p>This is a usage estimate, not a quote for a particular integration. Confirm your connection scope and any third-party costs before proceeding.</p></section>
        <section id="count"><h2>Count documents, not orders</h2><p>A purchase order, an order response, a despatch advice and an invoice are separate business documents. A workflow using all four exchanges four documents for one order. Your retailer may require a different set.</p><p>For illustration, 100 orders with four exchanged documents each means 400 documents. At the published standard rates, that is {formatPrice(400 * pricing.standard.documentFee)} in document fees plus the {pricingDisplay.monthlyFee} monthly mailbox fee: <strong>{formatPrice(pricing.standard.monthlyFee + 400 * pricing.standard.documentFee)} excluding VAT</strong>.</p><p>The pricing page describes each business document exchanged as counting once. Before estimating live usage, confirm how technical acknowledgements, failed deliveries, retries, test traffic and document corrections are treated. This guide does not assume a billing policy for those cases.</p></section>
        <section id="estimates"><h2>Example monthly estimates</h2><p>These examples use the standard published rates and assume the document volumes shown. They exclude VAT and any separate third-party charges.</p><table class="cost-table"><caption>Standard recurring estimates</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Documents per month</th><th scope="col">Document fees</th><th scope="col">Total including mailbox</th></tr></thead><tbody>{examples.map((example) => <tr><th scope="row">{example.documents.toLocaleString('en-GB')}</th><td>{example.usage}</td><td>{example.total}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p>For another volume, use the <a href="/pricing">EDI pricing calculator</a>. If your traffic is seasonal, estimate a quiet month and a peak month rather than relying on an annual average.</p></section>
        <section id="questions"><h2>Questions to settle before you choose</h2><ul><li>Which document types will each retailer require, and in which direction?</li><li>Does the proposed route need a separate ERP connector, automation subscription or network service?</li><li>Who owns mapping, retailer testing and ongoing changes, and what is included in the agreed scope?</li><li>When does the trial begin, what can you test during it, and what happens when it ends?</li><li>How will you see usage and check charges against exchanged documents?</li></ul><p>When comparing providers, request the same workflow and volume assumptions from each. A headline subscription price is difficult to compare if implementation, support or document usage are scoped differently.</p></section>
        <aside class="guide-callout"><h2>Bring your workflow and an estimated volume.</h2><p>We can review your retailer, business system and expected document flows before you make a commitment.</p><a class="button" href="/contact?intent=connection">Discuss your requirements</a></aside>
        <section class="guide-sources"><h2>Sources and limits</h2><p>Prices and published commercial terms come from <a href="/pricing">EDI Spark pricing</a>. Examples are calculated from the same price configuration as the calculator. Actual retailer requirements, connection scope and unsettled billing cases need confirmation. For the next step, use the <a href="/guides/retailer-edi-onboarding">retailer onboarding checklist</a>.</p></section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
